DCTelnet 2.0-UP/X (unofficial release, 1.11.2026)

An unofficial update of DCTelnet, the Telnet and BBS client for the Amiga,
based on upstream DCTelnet 2.0-dev by Bruno Frederic. It is not an official
release of the upstream project.

Highlights

- New built-in terminal renderer (default on 68020 and better): UTF-8,
  xterm, 256 colours, 24-bit RGB, mouse reports, bracketed paste, window
  titles and scrollback. The older renderers stay in Display > Renderer.
- SSH connections through the new ssh.library, plus Rlogin.
- PETSCII mode for Commodore 64 BBSes, with C64 fonts included.
- ANSI music, with Bell as Flash, Sound or Off.
- Per-BBS settings in the Address Book, SyncTERM phone book import,
  redial, keep alive and connect timeout.
- Select, copy and paste with the mouse; capture to file; save the screen
  as ANSI; find text in the scrollback.
- Display > 132 Columns, iCE Colours, an editor for the 16 ANSI colours
  and Display > Modern Icons for the tool bar.
- An ARexx port, and a login macro that waits for a text.
- RTG and 256-colour AGA screens, and a grey user interface on 16 colours.

The full list of changes is in the Docs drawer (CHANGES) and in the
History node of DCTelnet.guide.

Requirements

- Kickstart / Workbench v2.00 (V36) or higher
- A TCP/IP stack: AmiTCP, Roadshow, Miami, UAE bsdsocket.library or
  compatible

Installation

1. Download DCTelnet.lha from the GitHub releases section:
   https://github.com/spotUP/dctelnet/releases
2. Run the Installer script in the archive. On systems without the
   Installer tool, copy the files by hand as described in the Installation
   node of DCTelnet.guide.
